{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrwEzCNmMagvMbUp4uf8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I implemented the enrichment in `src/fromager/bootstrapper/_bootstrapper.py` and added the tests. `tests/test_bootstrapper_iterative.py` runs with 116 passed and 1 failed. The one failure, `TestPhasePrepareSource::test_constraint_logged_when_present`, also fails with my changes stashed, so I didn't touch it. I didn't run `ruff` because it isn't in `.venv`, so the new code hasn't been through the formatter.\n\n- **`_dependency_chain_suffix`:** it renders `\" (dependency chain: a==1 -> b==2 -> <wi.req>)\"` from `wi.why_snapshot`.\n- **`_enrich_resolution_error`:** for a `Resolve` item with a non-empty `why_snapshot`, a `ResolverException` stays a `ResolverException`. A `RuntimeError` stays a `RuntimeError`. Anything else becomes `RuntimeError(\"<TypeName>: <msg><suffix>\")`. Other phases and top-level requirements return the same `err` object.\n- **`_handle_phase_error`:** it enriches `err` before the test-mode, multiple-versions and normal-mode branches. Both bare `raise` statements are now `raise err`, so the enriched exception is raised with no `from` clause. The original is reachable through `__context__` and `__cause__` stays `None`.\n- **Subclasses:** I used plain `ResolverException` and `RuntimeError`, so a subclass of either (for example `ResolutionImpossible`) is replaced by the base type. If you want the subclass kept, say so.\n\nThe new tests (`TestResolutionErrorEnrichment`) cover the suffix format, all three exception shapes, the unchanged top-level and non-resolve cases, `__context__` and `__cause__` in normal mode, and the enriched error being recorded in test mode and multiple-versions mode."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1690,"cache_read_input_tokens":70737,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_